  message: "Conversational approval flow: human gave explicit 'I approve all of this and approve using auto-pr WITHOUT --gov' directive in conversation, so this PR proceeds via auto-pr instead of the standard governance approval workflow. Three artifacts in this PR: (1) the playbook file at .agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/twenty-pass-dogfood-procedure.md (~430 lines, six phases with sub-agent prompt templates, tranch-state schema, sentinel convention, recovery table, cost table, tmux fallback appendix), (2) AGENTS.md essentialization (2-sentence summary referencing the playbook), (3) hook tuple registered in .agent/hooks/_shared/on_transcript_change.py PLAYBOOKS list. No supervisor extension included — sub-agent architecture obsoletes the tmux-driver layer for this playbook, supervisor stays orthogonal for autonomous-mode respawn use."  # c219
